 {name:'Dhuhr',start:'After the Sun passes its highest point',meaning:'Solar noon has passed and the afternoon begins.',end:'Start of Asr',detail:'The clock time depends on longitude, date and the solar-noon calculation. Local mosques may add a precautionary interval.'},
 {name:'Asr',start:'Afternoon shadow criterion',meaning:'The earlier standard rule and later Hanafi rule use different shadow-length thresholds.',end:'Before sunset',detail:'The exact limits and late-prayer considerations require scholarly detail. Do not treat the sunset boundary as a reason to delay intentionally.'},
 {name:'Maghrib',start:'Sunset',meaning:'The Sun has disappeared below the horizon.',end:'Nightfall / Isha',detail:'Maghrib starts at sunset. In Ramadan, it is also the ordinary reference for iftar.'},
